<p>
  <%= trust.name %> respects your privacy. This policy explains what personal
  data we collect, why, and how we protect it, in line with the Digital
  Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 and the Information Technology Act, 2000.
</p>

<h2>1. Data we collect</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Account:</strong> name, email, mobile number and a securely hashed password (we never store your actual password).</li>
  <li><strong>Donations and membership:</strong> name, email, mobile number, amount, cause, payment mode, message and transaction ID.</li>
  <li><strong>Medical help requests:</strong> patient's name, Aadhaar number, date of birth, mobile number, email, illness, hospital and referrer's name.</li>
  <li><strong>Technical:</strong> a session cookie that keeps you logged in, and basic server logs (such as IP address) for security.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  We do not collect card numbers, UPI PINs or bank passwords. These are handled
  directly by our payment gateway, PayU.
</p>

<h2>2. Why we use it</h2>
<ul>
  <li>To process donations and memberships and send receipts and certificates.</li>
  <li>To review and respond to medical help requests.</li>
  <li>To run your account and show your history with the Trust.</li>
  <li>To keep accounts as required by law and to prevent fraud.</li>
</ul>
<p>We use your data only with your consent, which you give by ticking the consent box on our forms.</p>

<h2>3. How we protect it</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Stored records are encrypted (AES-256-GCM).</li>
  <li>Passwords are hashed with bcrypt.</li>
  <li>Only the last 4 digits of an Aadhaar number are printed on receipts.</li>
  <li>Admin access is limited to authorised trustees and protected by a password.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>PayU</strong>, to process payments.</li>
  <li><strong>Our email provider</strong>, to send receipts and replies.</li>
  <li>Government authorities, only when the law requires it.</li>
</ul>
<p>We never sell, rent or publish your personal data.</p>

<h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
<p>
  Donation and payment records are kept for at least 8 years, as required for
  a charitable trust's accounts and audits. Other data is kept only as long as
  needed for the purpose it was collected for.
</p>

<h2>6. Your rights</h2>
<p>
  You can ask us to see, correct or delete your personal data, or withdraw
  your consent, by contacting us. Records we must keep by law (such as
  donation records) cannot be deleted before the legal period ends.
</p>

<h2>7. Cookies</h2>
<p>
  We use one essential cookie to keep you logged in. We do not use advertising
  or tracking cookies.
</p>

<h2>8. Changes</h2>
<p>We may update this policy. The date at the top shows the latest version.</p>

